  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This makes 24 madeleines and takes about 30 minutes active work plus 1 hour of chilling. The thing to watch is the oven temperature: it must be properly hot before the batter goes in or you will not get the characteristic hump on the back of each cake."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brown the butter until it smells nutty. This beurre noisette is what gives madeleines their depth of flavour compared to versions made with plain melted butter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "unsalted-butter",
              "amount": 130,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "plus extra for greasing",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "plus extra for dusting",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lemon",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "zest only",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vanilla-extract",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Melt the butter in a small pan over medium heat, continuing to cook until it turns golden brown and smells nutty, about 5 minutes. Pour into a bowl and leave to cool slightly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk together the eggs, sugar, lemon zest, and vanilla until pale and slightly thickened, about 2 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fold in the flour and salt gently until just combined. Do not overmix."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fold in the cooled brown butter until the batter is smooth. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oven to 200C. Butter and flour a madeleine tin generously."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spoon the cold batter into the moulds, filling each about three-quarters full. Do not spread."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 10-12 minutes until the edges are golden and the hump in the centre has risen and set. Turn out immediately and cool on a rack. Best eaten within a few hours."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "No hump on the cakes",
              "cause": "Batter not cold enough or oven too cool",
              "fix": "Chill batter overnight and ensure oven is fully preheated to 200C before baking"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Madeleines are pale and dense",
              "cause": "Underbaked or butter not browned enough",
              "fix": "Bake until the edges are properly golden, not just set, and brown the butter to a deep hazelnut colour"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Madeleines stick in the tin",
              "cause": "Tin not buttered and floured thoroughly",
              "fix": "Coat every surface of the mould with butter then flour, tapping out the excess"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Madeleines come from the town of Commercy in the Lorraine region of northeastern France. They are forever linked with the writer Marcel Proust, who described one dipped in tea triggering a flood of childhood memories in his novel In Search of Lost Time. French patisseries sell them fresh throughout the day. They are best eaten within hours of baking, when the outside is just set and the inside still slightly soft."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
